    "question": {
      ":question/id": "afc39fd3-84b2-5384-bbf0-d2b5bc092e7d",
      ":question/problem": "Find $q$, if $5{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 19\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $q$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 5\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+q\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 19\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 19\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $q=-2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
